# clang-tidy configuration for the zsh-edit-select C agents.
#
# Scope: the hand-written agent sources in impl-x11/, impl-wayland/ and
# impl-wsl/ (Linux-compilable only; the mingw helper.exe and the macOS .m
# agent are outside clang-tidy's reach on Linux).  Generated wayland-scanner
# protocol .c files are not meant to be analyzed.
#
# Per-agent compile_commands.json is produced with:
#   cd <agent dir> && make clean && bear -- make CFLAGS='-O2 -DNDEBUG -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-parameter'
# (the CFLAGS override drops gcc-only flags such as -fipa-pta that break
# clang tooling; rebuild with plain `make` afterwards to restore the
# optimized native binary).
#
# Disabled checks, each triaged against the actual code (Jul 2026 pass):
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling
#     Flags every snprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), ...) / bounded memcpy.  All
#     call sites use correct explicit bounds; the *_s replacements do not
#     exist in glibc.  Pure noise.
#   clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy
#     Single site (resolve_helper_path): length is pre-validated against
#     sizeof(helper_path) immediately above the strcpy.  Safe.
#   bugprone-reserved-identifier / cert-dcl37-c / cert-dcl51-cpp
#     #define _GNU_SOURCE is a required libc feature-test macro.
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result
#     Comparisons against MAX_SELECTION_SIZE/MAX_CLIPBOARD_SIZE ((1024*1024)
#     etc.): the int multiplication cannot overflow and widening is
#     value-preserving.
#   bugprone-narrowing-conversions
#     size_t data_len -> int in XChangeProperty nelements: data_len is
#     hard-capped at 1 MB by MAX_SELECTION_SIZE, far below INT_MAX.
#   bugprone-branch-clone
#     Deliberate same-body branches with distinct conditions in
#     read_fd_with_timeout and the process_primary_update changed-detection
#     chain; kept separate for clarity of the EAGAIN/EOF/NULL cases.
#   bugprone-not-null-terminated-result
#     osc52_write frames a binary buffer with explicit lengths; NUL
#     termination is intentionally absent.
#   cert-err34-c
#     fscanf/sscanf integer parses check the return count and fall back to
#     time(NULL) / skip the message on failure; overflow pedantry only.
#     (The WSL win_seq "%lu" read is a documented leave-as-is: rewriting it
#     as "%*lu" trips gcc -Wformat=.)
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters, cert-err33-c
#     Style-tier noise; (void)-cast unchecked returns are the established
#     convention in these agents.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  cert-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -cert-dcl37-c,
  -cert-dcl51-cpp,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-not-null-terminated-result,
  -cert-err34-c,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cert-err33-c
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: ''
